        },
        {
          "chunk_id": "5776592c1d0a84b6_recursive_1",
          "text": ". ἄζωτον \"lifeless\"), which did not support either. Azote later became nitrogen in English, although it has kept the name in French and several other European languages.",
          "document_id": "5776592c1d0a84b6",
          "metadata": {
